  "slug": "intestinal-liver-mice-0dd6",
  "summary": "A batch of NAR database updates, plus canine and lung tumor atlases, refine where molecular evidence is anchored: CpGs, cell types, niches, kinase mutations.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the consolidation of heterogeneous molecular evidence into searchable, annotated resources at finer resolution. MethMarkerDB 2.0 covers methylation biomarkers across 21 cancer types and adds CpG-level and functional analysis modules. scGWAS-DB maps 3,649 GWAS datasets onto single-cell atlases spanning 74 tissues and 1,713 cell types. CROST 2.0 grows to 544 spatial transcriptomics projects (3,538 samples) and adds niche, colocalization and cancer-niche tools. KinaseMD 2.0 updates kinase mutation and drug-response annotations. Gene Expression Nebulas 2.0 extends standardized, manually curated transcriptomic profiles. iCellOmics joins multi-omic and literature-curated phenotype data for 17 industrially relevant cell lines. Cohort-scale atlases follow the same logic. The Canine Cancer Genome Atlas harmonizes 667 tumor-normal exome pairs and reports 39 drivers. A 1,824-tumor lung RNA-seq resource defines nine transcriptional clusters with an interactive portal. The kinetic-model and natural-product network studies are more peripheral, contributing reusable analytical frameworks rather than databases.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-15"
}
